WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.044
npm scripts are powerful because they give
projects a standard way to run build,

2
00:00:08.124 --> 00:00:13.641
test, lint, prepare, release, and
operational commands.

3
00:00:13.721 --> 00:00:20.927
Package lifecycle hooks can also run
automatically during installation or

4
00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:22.245
publishing.

5
00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:27.617
This power is useful, but it creates a
security concern:

6
00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:35.466
installing a package can become code
execution in the developer workstation or CI

7
00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:36.897
environment.

8
00:00:36.977 --> 00:00:42.269
That execution may have access to files,
network paths,

9
00:00:42.349 --> 00:00:47.753
and environment variables available to the
npm process.

10
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:53.801
Lifecycle script risk is especially
important in automation.

11
00:00:53.881 --> 00:00:59.961
CI systems often hold tokens, cloud
credentials, signing keys,

12
00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:05.670
deployment permissions, or access to
private registries.

13
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:11.493
If installation scripts run in a context
with broad secrets,

14
00:01:11.573 --> 00:01:17.653
a compromised dependency has a much more
valuable opportunity.

15
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:23.362
Teams should reduce secret exposure during
install steps,

16
00:01:23.442 --> 00:01:27.270
separate build and deploy permissions,

17
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:34.444
and avoid placing high-value credentials
in jobs that only need to restore

18
00:01:34.524 --> 00:01:35.987
dependencies.

19
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:42.260
Practical controls include reviewing
scripts in package.json,

20
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:48.420
watching for new install-time behavior in
dependency updates,

21
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:55.593
using least-privilege CI jobs, preferring
clean ephemeral build agents,

22
00:01:55.673 --> 00:02:03.442
and using install options that ignore
scripts where the workflow can tolerate it.

23
00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:11.291
Ignoring scripts is not universal because
some packages legitimately need build

24
00:02:11.371 --> 00:02:12.047
steps.

25
00:02:12.127 --> 00:02:19.783
The key is to know when code will execute
and to make that execution environment as

26
00:02:19.863 --> 00:02:22.340
constrained as possible.
